  "chapter": 489,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 55 Chapter 489\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 5562-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to manda-\n        tory testing in the event of a motor vehicle collision resulting\n        in injury or death\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend the Vehicle and Traffic  Law  (VTL)  to  mandate\nthat  when  an investigating officer arrives at the scene of an accident\nresulting in death or serious physical injury, the investigating officer\nmust ask the driver to take a field sobriety test when there are reason-\nable grounds to believe that the  driver  committed  a  serious  traffic\nviolation. If the driver refuses, the Department of Motor Vehicles would\nbe  authorized to suspend the driver's license pursuant to the processes\nand sanctions set forth under VTL Section 1194.\n \n  Impaired drivers who cause serious accidents must be held  accountable\nfor  their  actions.  As  originally  drafted,  however, the bill raises\nsignificant constitutional concerns that may allow impaired  drivers  to\navoid  being  held  responsible  for  their  actions.  The Executive has\nsecured an agreement with the Legislature to  pass  legislation  in  the\nupcoming  session  to  ensure the law can be implemented effectively. On\nthat basis, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2017
 },
